3869 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This below is the extender version of the description\050\050Step 1\nThe pilot begins in July 2026\054 with phased enforcement based on business size\056 Entities earning AED 50 million or more must comply first\054 followed by smaller VAT\055registered businesses and government bodies\056 B2C\055only businesses are excluded until further notice\056\n\nStep 2\nAll VAT\055registered businesses must appoint an FTA\055accredited ASP before implementation\056 The ASP converts invoices into XML or JSON and sends them securely to the Federal Tax Authority and buyers\056 Complete onboarding before July 2026 and ensure the ASP follows Peppol standards like UBL or PINT\056\n\nStep 3\nERP systems must create structured invoices in XML or JSON\054 map all fields to the Ministry\031s data dictionary\054 apply digital signatures\054 and link directly to the ASP\056 Manual or PDF invoices will no longer qualify as valid once e\055invoicing takes effect\056\n\nStep 4\nFrom July to December 2026\054 businesses should test system integration with the ASP and FTA sandbox\056 Verify data accuracy\054 run sample transactions\054 and train teams on new invoicing and reporting workflows to ensure readiness before full rollout\056\n\nStep 5\nE\055invoices and credit notes must be stored within the UAE as required by the Tax Procedures Law\056 Offshore or external hosting is prohibited\056 Implement secure archiving\054 access control\054 and retrieval processes to support audits and compliance\056\n\nStep 6\nUpdate VAT workflows for real\055time reporting and establish protocols for handling system issues\056 Any technical failure must be reported to the FTA within two business days\056 Train staff and budget for ASP integration\054 digital signatures\054 and compliance management to ensure a smooth transition\056)
     /K [ 92 ]
     /P 3870 0 R
     /Pg 3690 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

